            <ArticleTitle>GETTEMO position statement on bariatric endoscopic techniques as a voluntary medicine.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.17235/reed.2017.5144/2017</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dear Editor, We would like to clarify certain points in the article by C. Dolz et al. entitled &quot;Informed consent in digestive endoscopy - Patient information, endoscopist protection&quot;, more specifically regarding the section &quot;Obesity treatments&quot;. First, we want to congratulate the authors for their highly relevant yearlong research of the medico-legal aspects of Spanish endoscopy and for sharing their knowledge with endoscopists on a national level. With regard to the endoscopic management of obesity, we consider that the informed consent process should be even more comprehensive than that with other endoscopic techniques. As the author highlighted, there is less experience in some of these techniques.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
